  "label": "The text 'what if i told you' is mapped onto the bald Black man wearing sunglasses",
  "description": "The top text 'what if i told you' is positioned directly above the man's head, creating a visual and conceptual mapping where the speaker (implied by the text) is projected onto the visual entity of the man. This mapping leverages the man's serious, iconic appearance (Laurence Fishburne as Morpheus) to create a comedic or shocking contrast with the crude proposition in the lower text. The man becomes the 'you' or the implied subject of the proposition, making him the mapped entity for the textual phrase 'what if i told you'.",
